We investigate the influence of $b 	o c$ transitions on the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay in the $U_1$ leptoquark model, which is a well-known framework for explaining the observed anomalies in $b 	o c 	au  ar{
u}$ transitions. Our analysis reveals that the $b 	o c$ transitions have a significant impact on the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay rate, which is found to be suppressed by a factor of $0.1$ to $0.3$ compared to the standard model prediction. This suppression is attributed to the interference between the $b 	o c$ and $b 	o u$ transitions, which is a characteristic feature of the $U_1$ leptoquark model.
